.TH NEUROOS 1 "November 2026" "NeuroOS 0.1.0-alpha.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
neuroos \- local conversational Linux agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neuroos
setup | doctor [\-\-probe] | chat [\-\-plain] | feedback | backend start|stop|status
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs as an ordinary user. Model weights and a compatible local llama.cpp server
must be installed separately. No cloud inference or automatic model downloads.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Interactive private user configuration. No root or global security changes.
.TP
.B doctor
Check platform, dependencies, model, endpoint and rootless capabilities.
The optional probe sends a live constrained completion to the chosen backend.
.TP
.B chat
Persistent conversation; plain terminal mode is available without tmux.
.TP
.B feedback
Create a local sanitized diagnostic archive for inspection. Nothing is uploaded.
.TP
.B backend
Explicitly manage the optional bounded user inference service.
.SH FILES
User settings: XDG_CONFIG_HOME/neuroos/config.json.
User history: XDG_STATE_HOME/neuroos, or the directory selected during setup.
Both survive package removal; weights are never deleted by this package.
.SH SECURITY
Never run the agent as root. No SSH, network, boot, sudoers or global permission
changes are made. Linger is not enabled automatically. Alpha limitations apply.
.SH SEE ALSO
Documentation in /usr/share/doc/neuroos.
